  "limitations": [
    "These counts certify internal cache consistency, not complete source coverage, independent NCAA membership certification, or historical as-of availability.",
    "FBS-FCS scheduling is heavily selected: almost all recorded games are at FBS venues. A fitted division term is a conditional empirical association, not a causal estimate of division strength or a neutral-site win rate.",
    "Repaired older postseason coverage adds FBS-v-FBS only. Older FCS postseason and lower-division histories remain incomplete; a cross-division residual may absorb those coverage differences.",
    "2020 has only 127 source FBS nodes and three adjacent-year programs missing. Pandemic FCS spring schedules may be absent or season-coded differently; flag separately rather than assume comparability.",
    "Many lower-division nodes are unknown or sparse. Their results indirectly affect FCS and FBS network strength even when no FBS opponent has an unknown classification.",
    "FCS program resources and membership vary; one shared division term cannot justify a fixed per-team penalty or replace individual opponent results.",
    "End-season leave-one-game-out and chronological preweek ratings use different information sets and require separately evaluated calibration.",
    "2023-2025 have been inspected previously and are retrospective evaluation, not untouched prospective holdouts."
  ],
  "recommendedRobustnessChecks": [
    "Fit primary cross-division calibration after accounting for existing opponent-network rating difference and venue.",
    "Compare identical game targets under full-source and FBS/FCS-only context networks; this isolates sensitivity to lowerdivision context without relabeling FBS publication membership.",
    "Compare regular-season-only contexts between training and evaluation to assess the changing postseason coverage; never call this a correction to missing playoff facts.",
    "Treat2020 separately because of anomalous coverage, seasoncoding and pandemic schedules.",
    "Report subgroup game counts and venue imbalance, not just a pooled performance metric."
  ]
